---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research Teams | HUMANITY"
  description="A transparent early-stage hypothesis for source-linked event monitoring and research support."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="max-w-3xl border-b border-humanity-border pb-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Product discovery · Not for sale</p>
      <h1 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-6xl">
        Research from a clearer record.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
        HUMANITY is exploring whether source-linked event records can help
        research and editorial teams review what is known, what remains
        uncertain, and where each report came from.
      </p>
      <p
        class="mt-4 border-l-2 border-humanity-accent pl-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted"
      >
        This is an unvalidated product hypothesis—not a product offer,
        subscription, service commitment, or statement of customer demand. There
        is no account, checkout, paid API, or service-level guarantee.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section
      class="grid gap-5 border-b border-humanity-border py-9 md:grid-cols-3"
      aria-label="Potential future services"
    >
      <article class="card p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hypothesis 01</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Team monitoring
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          Possible saved topics, shared review queues, and alerts when
          source-linked records change.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold">
          Discovery range: $25–$100 per seat/month
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-humanity-textMuted">
          Illustrative interview prompt only; not a price or available plan.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hypothesis 02</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Research brief
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          A reviewed periodic brief for organizations, with event dates,
          evidence status, and links to original reporting.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold">
          Discovery range: $250–$1,000 per organization/month
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-humanity-textMuted">
          Illustrative interview prompt only; not a quote or commitment.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hypothesis 03</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Research data access
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
          Potential documented export or API for eligible records, subject to
          source rights and data quality.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold">No price set</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-humanity-textMuted">
          Rights, stable schemas, and operational support are not yet in place.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 py-9 md:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What exists today</p>
        <h2 class="editorial-title mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold">
          An early public research surface.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-humanity-textMuted">
        <p>
          The public site provides browsable published records, source links,
          event search and filters, a map of published locations, and
          methodology and source-transparency pages. Coverage is incomplete, and
          the published feed may be empty when no candidate meets the existing
          evidence and publication requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          Commercial use cannot be evaluated until source-specific storage,
          quotation, attribution, commercial-use, and redistribution rights have
          been reviewed. No evidence threshold will be lowered to create a
          larger catalog.
        </p>
        <a href="/methodology" class="link inline-block"
          >Read the evidence and publication method →</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-t border-humanity-border py-8">
      <h2 class="editorial-title text-2xl font-semibold">
        What would need validation
      </h2>
      <ul
        class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm text-humanity-textMuted sm:grid-cols-2"
      >
        <li>Interviews with researchers, editors, and civil-society teams</li>
        <li>Repeated evidence of a real monitoring or review problem</li>
        <li>Reliable ingestion and correction workflows</li>
        <li>Legal review of source rights and privacy obligations</li>
        <li>Operational cost, support, and security assessment</li>
        <li>Clear value beyond the free public record</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
